# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TINYFISH_API_KEY is the only thing you need.
#
# Get a key at https://agent.tinyfish.ai/api-keys
# Copy this file to .env and fill it in, or just export it inline:
#     export TINYFISH_API_KEY=sk-tinyfish-...
#
# Everything else in this file is optional. With no LLM configured, BrandKit
# runs its deterministic core, which is the default and the recommended mode.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
TINYFISH_API_KEY=sk-tinyfish-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Port for the local server (default 3000)
# PORT=3000

# ===========================================================================
# OPTIONAL: LLM narration layer
# ===========================================================================
#
# TinyFish Search and Fetch read the live web. Neither is a language model, and
# neither can write prose. So BrandKit splits the two jobs:
#
#   - The deterministic core (colour, type, contrast, CIEDE2000, the token
#     graph, sentence-level voice measurement) is computed locally from
#     fetched bytes. It needs no key and is what the demo runs.
#   - An LLM, when configured, only *narrates*: a tone paragraph, message
#     pillars, writing guidance. It is structurally barred from touching
#     colour, type or logo values.
#
# Pick one of the two blocks below. Leave both commented out and BrandKit runs
# without narration.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option A — Google Gemini
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
# A key is the only thing required. Without a model, the current stable flagship
# is used, so the shortest useful config is a single line:
#
#     GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza...
#
# GEMINI_MODEL is the model to use. The text models available today:
#
#   gemini-3.8-flash        current stable flagship; the default here
#   gemini-3.5-flash-lite   cheapest and fastest of the 3.x line
#   gemini-3.7-flash        previous-generation Flash, complex multi-step work
#   gemini-3.6-flash        previous-generation Flash, balanced
#   gemini-3.5-flash        legacy Flash, routine high-volume work
#   gemini-3.1-flash-lite   frontier-class quality, fraction of the cost
#   gemini-3.1-pro-preview  preview Pro; highest capability, tighter rate limits
#
# Model ids change often — Google ships a new one every few weeks and retires
# old ones. The live list is https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models, and an
# unknown id is reported by name rather than as a bare 404.
#
# GEMINI_THINKING_LEVEL tunes how much the model reasons before answering
# (minimal, low, medium, high). Gemini 3 thinks by default, which costs latency
# and output tokens for narration, so this defaults to `low` and only needs
# raising if you want a harder read on positioning.
#
# GEMINI_BASE_URL is almost always left alone. It exists for Vertex-compatible
# gateways and for testing; the default is Google's own endpoint.
#
# GOOGLE_API_KEY is accepted as a synonym for GEMINI_API_KEY, because Google uses
# both names in its own documentation. LLM_MODEL also works in place of
# GEMINI_MODEL, so one variable can switch models on either provider below.
#
# GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza...
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash
# GEMINI_THINKING_LEVEL=low
# GEMINI_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option B — any OpenAI-compatible endpoint
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# All three variables are required together. The request is a standard Chat
# Completions call:
#
#   OpenAI       https://api.openai.com/v1          gpt-4o-mini
#   Groq         https://api.groq.com/openai/v1     llama-3.3-70b-versatile
#   OpenRouter   https://openrouter.ai/api/v1       google/gemini-flash-1.5
#   Together     https://api.together.xyz/v1        meta-llama/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct-Turbo
#   DeepSeek     https://api.deepseek.com/v1        deepseek-chat
#   Mistral      https://api.mistral.ai/v1          mistral-small-latest
#   xAI          https://api.x.ai/v1                grok-2-latest
#   Cerebras     https://api.cerebras.ai/v1         llama3.1-8b
#   Ollama       http://localhost:11434/v1         llama3.2   (no real key needed)
#
# Gemini is reachable this way too, through Google's OpenAI-compatible surface,
# if you would rather keep everything on one variable set:
#
#   LLM_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
#   LLM_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which provider runs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# LLM_PROVIDER is optional and only needed to break a tie or to be explicit:
#
#   unset        a complete Option B trio wins; otherwise a Gemini key is used
#   gemini       always use Gemini, and fail loudly if its key is missing
#   openai       always use the Option B trio, and name anything missing
#
# An unrecognised value is an error rather than a silent fallback, so a typo in
# this file can never leave you wondering why narration never appeared.
#
# LLM_PROVIDER=gemini
#
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-...
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini